From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KmsFbErr <kmsfberr@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 04:35:00 
Subject: [PATCH 0119] gpu31-kms: fbdev postcondition failure at KERN_ERR (int75, module-only)

The int74 run's dmesg was flooded with userspace faults, so the fb0 failure
reason was lost.  In addition to the full dev_err line and the register dump,
the failure now emits an explicit pr_err with crtc id/enabled/active/
primary->state->fb/wanted fb, which lands in the persisted 256 KB trace even
when the rest is drowned out.  Module-only (fbdev slice).

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos_drm7580_fbdev.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos_drm7580_fbdev.c
@@ -164,6 +164,12 @@
 			ex->crtc.primary && ex->crtc.primary->state ?
 				ex->crtc.primary->state->fb : NULL,
 			ex->crtc.primary ? ex->crtc.primary->fb : NULL, fb);
+		/* int75: keep the reason at KERN_ERR in the persisted trace. */
+		pr_err("exynos7580: fbdev scanout failed: crtc id=%u enabled=%d active=%d primary->state->fb=%p want=%p\n",
+		       ex->crtc.base.id, ex->crtc.enabled,
+		       ex->crtc.state ? ex->crtc.state->active : -1,
+		       ex->crtc.primary && ex->crtc.primary->state ?
+				ex->crtc.primary->state->fb : NULL, fb);
 		/* int70: name the register state that made the check fail. */
 		decon_kms_log_state(ex->decon, "fbdev scanout failed");
 		return -EIO;
